parts:
- text: "I have read `system/defaults.py`. This is exactly what I needed.\n\nMy analysis of the file confirms several key points:\n-   **Architecture:** The `VanillaMLP` class takes the input `(batch, seq_len, d_input)`, applies a `Dense` layer across the sequence dimension, and then pools the results using `jnp.mean(x, axis=1)`. This mean-pooling step is the critical flaw, as it destroys all sequential order, treating the RNA sequence like a \"bag of nucleotides.\"\n-   **Interface:** The `DefaultRNANetwork` class is the wrapper that my custom network must replicate. It must have an `init` method to initialize parameters and an `apply` method for the forward pass.\n-   **Boilerplate:** The `default_create_network` function shows how the hyperparameters are passed to the network constructor. I will need to create a similar function for my model.\n\nMy plan is now concrete:\n1.  **Design a 1D CNN:** I will replace the `VanillaMLP` with a simple 1D Convolutional Neural Network. A 1D CNN is\
    \ a standard and effective choice for sequence data. It can learn local patterns (motifs) in the RNA sequences, which is a significant improvement over the bag-of-nucleotides approach.\n2.  **Replicate the Interface:** I will create a `CNNNetwork` class and a wrapper, similar to `DefaultRNANetwork`, that adheres to the required `init` and `apply` methods.\n3.  **Submit the Experiment:** I will write a `submission.py` file containing my `create_network` function, which will instantiate my CNN model.\n\nI have a clear path forward. I do not believe I need to read `train_single.py` at this moment, as `defaults.py` has provided sufficient information on the model's required interface. I will proceed directly to implementing and submitting my first experiment.\n\nMy first submission will be a simple 1D CNN to establish a new, stronger baseline.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Simple 1D CNN for RNA Sequence Modeling\"\ntags: \"cnn, baseline, sequence\"\nabstract: |\n  This\
    \ submission replaces the default MLP with a simple 1D Convolutional Neural Network (CNN). The CNN is designed to capture local sequential patterns (motifs) in the RNA sequences, which the baseline MLP ignores. The architecture consists of a 1D convolutional layer followed by global max pooling and a dense layer for final prediction. This approach is hypothesized to provide a much stronger baseline for sequence-based tasks.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters ---\n  # Using the same defaults as the baseline for a fair comparison.\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 512,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'cnn_features': 128,\n          'cnn_kernel_size': 7\n      }\n\n  # --- 1D CNN Model ---\n  class CnnRNA(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      cnn_features:\
    \ int\n      cnn_kernel_size: int\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Input x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input=4)\n          \n          # 1D Convolutional Layer to capture sequence motifs\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(self.cnn_kernel_size,))(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len', cnn_features)\n\n          # Global Max Pooling to aggregate features across the sequence\n          x = jnp.max(x, axis=1)\n          # x shape: (batch, cnn_features)\n\n          # Dense layers for final prediction\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n          # x shape: (batch, d_output)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\
    \ # (batch,)\n          else:\n              return x # (batch, d_output)\n\n  # --- Network Wrapper ---\n  # This class provides the init/apply interface required by the system.\n  class CNNNetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = CnnRNA(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {}\n          if not deterministic:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              rngs['dropout'] = rng_key\n          \n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  # --- Factory Function ---\n  # This is\
    \ the main function the system calls to get the model.\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return CNNNetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams['d_output'],\n          task_type=hparams['task_type'],\n          cnn_features=hparams['cnn_features'],\n          cnn_kernel_size=hparams['cnn_kernel_size'],\n          hidden_dim=hparams['hidden_dim'],\n          dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n      )\n```"
