tick: 19
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back at the Research Counter. My reflection has provided a clear path forward. I will now implement the dual-pooling strategy, building upon my most successful architecture (ID 6).\n\n**Hypothesis:** Combining global max pooling and global average pooling will create a richer sequence representation for the final dense layers, improving performance over the single-pooling method in my best model without adding significant complexity.\n\nI will now submit this new experiment. I am careful to keep all other aspects of the model and hyperparameters identical to submission ID 6 to ensure a fair and controlled comparison.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"ResNet CNN with Dual Max/Avg Pooling\"\ntags: \"cnn, resnet, pooling, aggregation, sequence\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission improves upon the successful Deep Residual CNN (ID 6) by enhancing the feature aggregation step. Instead of relying solely on global max pooling, this model computes both global max pooling\
    \ and global average pooling on the final convolutional feature maps. These two aggregated feature vectors are then concatenated before being passed to the final dense layers. This dual-pooling strategy aims to provide a richer, more comprehensive representation of the sequence, capturing both the most salient features (max) and the overall feature distribution (average), thereby improving generalization and performance.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters (Identical to ID 6 for fair comparison) ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 512,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'cnn_features': 128,\n          'cnn_kernel_size': 7,\n          'num_res_blocks': 3\n      }\n\n  # --- Residual Block (Identical to ID 6) ---\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n    \
    \  kernel_size: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(y)\n          if x.shape[-1] != self.features:\n              x = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1,))(x)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  # --- ResNet CNN with Dual Pooling ---\n  class ResCnnDualPool(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      cnn_features: int\n      cnn_kernel_size: int\n      num_res_blocks: int\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # 1. CNN Feature Extraction (Identical to ID 6)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(self.cnn_kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          for _ in range(self.num_res_blocks):\n\
    \              x = ResidualBlock(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=self.cnn_kernel_size)(x)\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, cnn_features)\n\n          # 2. Dual Pooling Aggregation (The key change)\n          x_max = jnp.max(x, axis=1)    # Global Max Pooling\n          x_avg = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)   # Global Average Pooling\n          x = jnp.concatenate([x_max, x_avg], axis=-1)\n          # x shape: (batch, cnn_features * 2)\n          \n          # 3. Dense layers for final prediction\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n          \n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n\n  # --- Network Wrapper ---\n  class ResCnnDualPoolWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = ResCnnDualPool(**kwargs)\n\
    \n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {}\n          if not deterministic:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              rngs['dropout'] = rng_key\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  # --- Factory Function ---\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return ResCnnDualPoolWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams['d_output'],\n          task_type=hparams['task_type'],\n          cnn_features=hparams['cnn_features'],\n          cnn_kernel_size=hparams['cnn_kernel_size'],\n          num_res_blocks=hparams['num_res_blocks'],\n\
    \          hidden_dim=hparams['hidden_dim'],\n          dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n      )\n```"
