tick: 35
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am ready to implement my new hybrid 1D-2D architecture. This is my most complex model yet, but it is grounded in a strong, domain-aware hypothesis.\n\n**The Plan:**\n1.  **Create Pairwise Map:** I'll write a helper function that takes the one-hot encoded sequence `(L, 4)` and computes an `(L, L, 2)` map representing potential canonical (A-U, G-C) and wobble (G-U) base pairings.\n2.  **1D Branch:** I will use my best-performing 1D architecture (Dilated ResNet) as the sequence feature extractor.\n3.  **2D Branch:** I will implement a simple 2D CNN (a few convolutional layers followed by pooling) to process the pairwise map.\n4.  **Fusion:** The outputs of both branches will be concatenated and passed to a final MLP for prediction.\n\nThis first attempt will be a proof of concept. If it shows promise, I can refine the 2D architecture and the pairwise map creation in future iterations.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid 1D-2D Structure-Aware Model\"\ntags: \"hybrid\
    \ model, 2d cnn, rna structure, dilated convolution, resnet\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission introduces a novel hybrid architecture that processes both 1D sequence data and a 2D representation of RNA secondary structure. A helper function computes a pairwise map of potential base pairings (canonical and wobble) from the input sequence. The model has two branches: 1) a powerful 1D Dilated ResNet to extract sequence features, and 2) a simple 2D CNN to extract structural features from the pairwise map. The feature vectors from both branches are concatenated and passed to a final prediction head. This structure-aware approach is a significant departure from previous models and is hypothesized to achieve a new level of performance by incorporating domain-specific biological knowledge as an inductive bias.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters ---\n  def\
    \ _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'hidden_dim': 512, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'cnn_features_1d': 256, 'cnn_kernel_size_1d': 7, 'num_res_blocks_1d': 3,\n          'dilation_rates': [1, 2, 4],\n          'cnn_features_2d': 64, 'cnn_kernel_size_2d': 5\n      }\n\n  # --- Helper to create Pairwise Map ---\n  def create_pairwise_map(x):\n      # x shape: (batch, seq_len, 4) where 4 is one-hot for A, U, C, G\n      seq_len = x.shape[1]\n      \n      # Outer product to get all pairwise combinations\n      # a[i,k]*a[j,l] gives pairing of base k at pos i with base l at pos j\n      pairwise_matrix = jnp.einsum('bik,bjk->bijkl', x, x)\n      \n      # Canonical pairs: A-U (0,1), U-A (1,0), G-C (3,2), C-G (2,3)\n      au = pairwise_matrix[:, :, :, 0, 1]\n      ua = pairwise_matrix[:, :, :, 1, 0]\n      gc = pairwise_matrix[:, :, :, 3, 2]\n      cg = pairwise_matrix[:, :, :, 2, 3]\n      canonical = au + ua + gc + cg\n      \n      # Wobble\
    \ pairs: G-U (3,1), U-G (1,3)\n      gu = pairwise_matrix[:, :, :, 3, 1]\n      ug = pairwise_matrix[:, :, :, 1, 3]\n      wobble = gu + ug\n      \n      # Stack to create (batch, seq_len, seq_len, 2) map\n      return jnp.stack([canonical, wobble], axis=-1)\n\n  # --- 1D CNN Tower ---\n  class CnnEncoder1D(nn.Module):\n      features: int; kernel_size: int; num_res_blocks: int; dilation_rates: Sequence[int]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          for i in range(self.num_res_blocks):\n              dilation = self.dilation_rates[i] if i < len(self.dilation_rates) else self.dilation_rates[-1]\n              x = DilatedResidualBlock1D(features=self.features, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dilation=dilation)(x)\n          x_max = jnp.max(x, axis=1)\n          x_avg = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n          return jnp.concatenate([x_max, x_avg], axis=-1)\n\
    \n  class DilatedResidualBlock1D(nn.Module):\n      features: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y); y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,), padding='SAME')(y)\n          if x.shape[-1] != self.features: x = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1,))(x)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  # --- 2D CNN Tower ---\n  class CnnEncoder2D(nn.Module):\n      features: int; kernel_size: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, p):\n          p = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size, self.kernel_size), padding='SAME')(p)\n          p = nn.relu(p)\n          p = nn.Conv(features=self.features*2, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size, self.kernel_size), padding='SAME')(p)\n          p = nn.relu(p)\n\
    \          # Global pooling for 2D\n          p = jnp.max(p, axis=(1, 2))\n          return p\n\n  # --- Hybrid Model ---\n  class HybridModel(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # 1. Create 2D map\n          pairwise_map = create_pairwise_map(x)\n          # 2. 1D Branch\n          encoder_1d = CnnEncoder1D(features=self.hparams['cnn_features_1d'], kernel_size=self.hparams['cnn_kernel_size_1d'],\n                                    num_res_blocks=self.hparams['num_res_blocks_1d'], dilation_rates=self.hparams['dilation_rates'])\n          features_1d = encoder_1d(x)\n          # 3. 2D Branch\n          encoder_2d = CnnEncoder2D(features=self.hparams['cnn_features_2d'], kernel_size=self.hparams['cnn_kernel_size_2d'])\n          features_2d = encoder_2d(pairwise_map)\n          # 4. Fusion\n          combined_features = jnp.concatenate([features_1d, features_2d], axis=-1)\n          # 5. Prediction Head\n\
    \          y = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['hidden_dim'])(combined_features)\n          y = nn.relu(y); y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_output'])(y)\n          if self.hparams['task_type'] == \"regression\": return y.squeeze(-1)\n          else: return y\n\n  # --- Network Wrapper ---\n  class HybridWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams): self.network = HybridModel(hparams=hparams)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {}; rngs['dropout'] = rng_key if rng_key is not None else random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams:\
    \ Dict[str, Any]): return HybridWrapper(hparams)\n```"
