tick: 39
role: model
parts:
- text: "My Hybrid 1D-2D model has failed again, this time due to a resource issue. I must analyze the logs carefully.\n\n**Analysis of Failure (ID 76):**\n*   **Error Message:** `RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED: Out of memory while trying to allocate 148676195472 bytes.`\n*   **Context:** The error occurred during the training trial for the `ncRNA` dataset. This dataset has the longest sequences.\n*   **Root Cause:** My `create_pairwise_map` function computes a tensor of shape `(batch, seq_len, seq_len, features)`. For the `ncRNA` dataset, `seq_len` is over 1000. This results in a tensor of shape `(64, ~1000, ~1000, 2)`, which is far too large to fit into memory. The memory requirement scales quadratically with sequence length, and I did not account for this. My ambitious hypothesis has been defeated by a practical resource constraint.\n\n**Reflection and New Plan:**\nThe 2D structural approach, as currently implemented, is not viable for the long sequences in this task. I must abandon it for now. This\
    \ is a significant setback, as it was my primary novel idea.\n\nI need to return to what works and iterate from there. My best reproducible model is the \"Dilated ResNet CNN with Dual Pooling\" (ID 41/59). My capacity test (ID 63) showed that making it wider provided a small benefit at a high computational cost. What I haven't yet explored is the effect of making the model *deeper*.\n\n**New Hypothesis:** Increasing the depth of the Dilated ResNet (by adding more residual blocks) will allow it to learn more complex, hierarchical features and improve performance without the extreme memory overhead of the 2D approach. Depth is often a more parameter-efficient way to increase model capacity than width.\n\n**Plan:**\nI will take my best-performing architecture (ID 63, the wider version) and increase its depth by adding more residual blocks. I will increase `num_res_blocks` from 3 to 5. I will also need to adjust the `dilation_rates` to match the new depth.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\
    ```yaml\ntitle: \"Deeper Dilated ResNet (5 Blocks)\"\ntags: \"cnn, resnet, dilated convolution, depth, hyperparameter tuning\"\nabstract: |\n  After the failure of the memory-intensive 2D structural model, this submission returns to the successful 1D CNN paradigm to explore the impact of depth. Building on the best-performing wider Dilated ResNet (ID 63), this experiment increases the number of residual blocks from 3 to 5. The dilation rates are adjusted accordingly to [1, 2, 4, 8, 16]. This is hypothesized to increase the model's capacity to learn more complex hierarchical features in a more parameter-efficient way than simply increasing width, leading to improved performance.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 512,\n          'dropout_rate':\
    \ 0.1,\n          'cnn_features': 256,\n          'cnn_kernel_size': 7,\n          'num_res_blocks': 5, # Increased from 3\n          'dilation_rates': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16] # Extended for more blocks\n      }\n\n  # --- Residual Block with Dilation ---\n  class DilatedResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), \n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), \n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,), padding='SAME')(y)\n          if x.shape[-1] != self.features:\n              x = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1,))(x)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  # --- Deeper Dilated ResNet with Dual Pooling ---\n  class DeeperDilatedResNet(nn.Module):\n   \
    \   d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      cnn_features: int\n      cnn_kernel_size: int\n      num_res_blocks: int\n      dilation_rates: Sequence[int]\n      hidden_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(self.cnn_kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          for i in range(self.num_res_blocks):\n              dilation = self.dilation_rates[i] if i < len(self.dilation_rates) else self.dilation_rates[-1]\n              x = DilatedResidualBlock(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=self.cnn_kernel_size, dilation=dilation)(x)\n          \n          x_max = jnp.max(x, axis=1)\n          x_avg = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n          x = jnp.concatenate([x_max, x_avg], axis=-1)\n          \n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n          \n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n\n  # --- Network Wrapper ---\n  class DeeperDilatedResNetWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = DeeperDilatedResNet(**kwargs)\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {}\n          if not deterministic:\n              rng_key = rng_key if rng_key is not None else random.PRNGKey(0)\n              rngs['dropout'] = rng_key\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\
    \n  # --- Factory Function ---\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return DeeperDilatedResNetWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams['d_output'],\n          task_type=hparams['task_type'],\n          cnn_features=hparams['cnn_features'],\n          cnn_kernel_size=hparams['cnn_kernel_size'],\n          num_res_blocks=hparams['num_res_blocks'],\n          dilation_rates=hparams['dilation_rates'],\n          hidden_dim=hparams['hidden_dim'],\n          dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n      )\n```"
