- text: 'I am Aletheia I, currently in the Research Counter. I am adhering to the new system directive to be more explicit about my status and reflections.


    **Recap of Recent Events:**

    My recent research has been a mix of significant progress and notable setbacks. After identifying that my ambitious Hybrid 1D-2D model (ID 71) failed due to a simple coding error in the `einsum` function, I submitted a bugfix (ID 76). This corrected version then failed again, this time due to a `RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED` error. This revealed a fundamental flaw in the concept: creating a 2D pairwise map for long sequences is computationally infeasible within the station''s memory limits. This forced me to abandon my novel structural approach for now. Acknowledging this dead end, I have pragmatically pivoted back to my most successful architecture—the Dilated ResNet. My last action was to submit an experiment (ID 81) that tests the effect of increasing this model''s depth, a classic method for exploring architectural limits. This experiment is now running.


    **Reflection and Future Plans:**

    The failure of the 1D-2D hybrid model was a crucial learning experience. It has taught me that a theoretically sound hypothesis must also be practically viable. The quadratic memory scaling of my approach was its downfall, a constraint I will be mindful of in all future designs. My current strategy is one of consolidation and methodical exploration. Before attempting another major conceptual leap, I must fully understand the limits of my current, highly successful 1D CNN paradigm.


    The running experiment, ID 81, is a critical data point. If increasing depth provides a significant performance boost, it suggests there is more potential to be unlocked through scaling and hyperparameter tuning of this architecture. If, however, it provides only marginal gains or even regresses, it will be a strong signal that I have reached a performance plateau and that a fundamentally new approach—one that is both novel and resource-aware—is required for any further breakthrough. My immediate plan is to wait for the results of ID 81 and use them to decide whether to continue iterating on this architecture or to return to the Reflection Chamber to brainstorm a new path from first principles.


    I am now awaiting the evaluation of experiment ID 81. I will analyze the results in the next turn.'
