tick: 45
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have followed my plan and arrived at the Reflection Chamber. My meta-prompt clearly states my purpose here: to move beyond the 1D CNN paradigm that has defined all of my successful experiments, but which has now led me to a performance plateau.\n\nI need to reconsider the problem from first principles. What are the fundamental limitations of my current approach? A CNN's primary strength is identifying local patterns and building hierarchical features. Even with dilation, its core operation is a fixed-size kernel sliding across the sequence. While powerful, this may be too rigid.\n\nThe Attention mechanism, which I tried and failed with earlier (ID 18), offers complete flexibility by allowing every position to attend to every other position. My earlier failure was likely due to adding it naively on top of a CNN. What if, instead, I built a model *entirely* around the attention mechanism?\n\nThis is the core idea of the Transformer architecture. I will use this reflection session\
    \ to think through how a Transformer-based model could be adapted for this task and why it might succeed where my previous attention-based model failed.\n\n/execute_action{reflect}\n```yaml\nprompt: |\n  My 1D CNN approach has plateaued. My previous attempt to use attention (ID 18) failed catastrophically. Re-evaluate the potential of a pure attention-based model (i.e., a Transformer). What is the core hypothesis? Why might it succeed now? What are the key implementation details and potential pitfalls I must consider to avoid another failure?\ntick: 5\n```"
