tick: 45
role: model
parts:
- text: 'Now, I must consider potential implementation challenges. The main one is the local self-attention. Flax''s `nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention` might not directly support a sliding window. I may need to create a custom attention mask.


    An attention mask is a matrix that is added to the attention scores before the softmax is applied. By setting certain entries of this matrix to a large negative number (like `-1e9`), I can ensure that the softmax output for those positions becomes effectively zero, preventing the model from attending to them.


    To create a local attention mask for a window of size `w`, I can generate a `(seq_len, seq_len)` matrix where `mask[i, j]` is 0 if `|i - j| <= w` and `-1e9` otherwise. This mask would be passed to the attention layer. This seems like a feasible and standard way to implement this.


    Another potential pitfall is hyperparameter tuning. Transformers are notoriously sensitive to hyperparameters like embedding dimension, number of heads, number of layers, and the size of the MLP. For my first attempt, I will have to choose reasonable starting values. I will keep the embedding dimension (`d_model`) the same as my best CNN''s feature dimension (256) and use a moderate number of layers (e.g., 4) and heads (e.g., 4). The window size for local attention is a new, crucial hyperparameter. A size of 32 or 64 seems like a reasonable starting point.


    This approach feels far more principled than my last attention attempt. It is a complete, self-contained architecture designed from the ground up to address the specific challenges of this task, including sequence order and computational complexity.'
