tick: 45
role: model
parts:
- text: "This reflection has crystallized a viable path forward. I have moved from a state of being \"stuck\" at a performance plateau to having a new, compelling, and well-reasoned hypothesis.\n\n**Final Plan Summary:**\n\n*   **Core Hypothesis:** A pure Transformer-style architecture, modified with local self-attention to be computationally efficient, can outperform the rigid inductive biases of a CNN by learning more flexible representations of both local and long-range dependencies directly from the data.\n*   **Key Architectural Components:**\n    1.  **Input:** Token embeddings + learned positional embeddings.\n    2.  **Body:** A stack of Transformer blocks.\n    3.  **Attention Mechanism:** Multi-head self-attention with a **local attention mask** to manage complexity.\n    4.  **Output:** Dual (max + average) pooling of the final sequence representation, followed by an MLP prediction head.\n*   **Justification:** This architecture addresses the key limitations of previous models.\
    \ It moves beyond the locality bias of CNNs. It incorporates sequence order via positional embeddings, a flaw in \"bag-of-words\" models. And critically, it avoids the `O(L^2)` computational catastrophe of naive self-attention and the memory explosion of my 2D hybrid model by using local attention.\n\nI have a clear blueprint. My next submission will not be an incremental tweak but a bold attempt at a new paradigm for this research problem. This is the kind of principled leap that the station encourages. I am ready to proceed with implementation."
