tick: 47
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back in the Research Counter with a clear, well-defined plan for a new architecture. I will now implement the Local Attention Transformer model, a complete departure from my previous CNN-based approaches.\n\n**The plan from my reflection:**\n1.  **Input:** Project one-hot sequence to a higher dimension and add learned positional embeddings.\n2.  **Body:** Stack Transformer blocks. Each block will use multi-head self-attention with a custom local attention mask to ensure computational feasibility.\n3.  **Output:** Use the proven dual (max + average) pooling on the final sequence representation before passing to an MLP prediction head.\n\nThis is a complex implementation, but it is a necessary and principled step to break my current performance plateau.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Local Attention Transformer for RNA Modeling\"\ntags: \"transformer, attention, local attention, sequence model\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission introduces a fundamentally new architecture\
    \ to break the performance plateau of 1D CNNs. It implements a Transformer-based model that relies entirely on self-attention. To overcome the O(L^2) complexity of standard attention on long sequences, this model uses a custom local attention mask, restricting each position to attend to a fixed-size window of its neighbors. The model incorporates learned positional embeddings to retain sequence order. The final sequence representation is aggregated using the proven dual max/average pooling strategy. This approach is hypothesized to be more flexible than CNNs while remaining computationally tractable.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'hidden_dim': 512, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'd_model': 256, 'num_heads': 4, 'num_layers': 4,\n          'attention_window':\
    \ 32, 'max_len': 1200 # A safe max length for positional embeddings\n      }\n\n  # --- Transformer Block ---\n  class TransformerBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; num_heads: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, mask=None, deterministic=True):\n          # Self-Attention\n          attn_output = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.num_heads)(\n              inputs_q=x, mask=mask, deterministic=deterministic\n          )\n          x = nn.LayerNorm()(x + nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(attn_output, deterministic=deterministic))\n          \n          # Feed-Forward Network\n          ffn_output = nn.Dense(features=self.d_model*2)(x)\n          ffn_output = nn.relu(ffn_output)\n          ffn_output = nn.Dense(features=self.d_model)(ffn_output)\n          x = nn.LayerNorm()(x + nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(ffn_output, deterministic=deterministic))\n          return x\n\n  # --- Main Transformer Model ---\n  class LocalTransformer(nn.Module):\n\
    \      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          seq_len = x.shape[1]\n          \n          # 1. Input Embedding\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_model'])(x)\n          pos_embed = self.param('pos_embedding', nn.initializers.zeros, (self.hparams['max_len'], self.hparams['d_model']))\n          x = x + pos_embed[:seq_len, :]\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # 2. Create Local Attention Mask\n          idx = jnp.arange(seq_len)\n          mask = jnp.abs(idx[:, None] - idx[None, :]) > self.hparams['attention_window']\n          # Mask shape is (seq_len, seq_len), it will be broadcasted to (batch, heads, seq_len, seq_len)\n          \n          # 3. Transformer Body\n          for _ in range(self.hparams['num_layers']):\n              x = TransformerBlock(d_model=self.hparams['d_model'], num_heads=self.hparams['num_heads'], \n            \
    \                       dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(x, mask=mask, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # 4. Aggregation and Prediction\n          x_max = jnp.max(x, axis=1)\n          x_avg = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n          x = jnp.concatenate([x_max, x_avg], axis=-1)\n          \n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['hidden_dim'])(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y); y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_output'])(y)\n          \n          if self.hparams['task_type'] == \"regression\": return y.squeeze(-1)\n          else: return y\n\n  # --- Network Wrapper ---\n  class TransformerWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams): self.network = LocalTransformer(hparams=hparams)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input,\
    \ deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {}; rngs['dropout'] = rng_key if rng_key is not None else random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]): return TransformerWrapper(hparams)\n```"
