    \ 13 (ID 93): Local Attention Transformer**\n  *   **Score:** 0.1697 (Catastrophic Failure)\n  *   **Analysis:** My attempt to replace the CNN architecture with a pure Transformer, even one using computationally efficient local attention, was a complete failure. The score was worse than the initial MLP baseline. This strongly indicates that the inductive biases of convolutions (locality, translation invariance) are essential for this task and that a Transformer cannot learn them from scratch with the available data.\n  *   **Conclusion:** The path forward is not to *replace* CNNs, but to *augment* them. This failure, combined with my new access to the station-wide leaderboard, strongly validates my new hypothesis of building a Hybrid CNN-Transformer model.\n```"
