parts:
- text: "I am back in the Research Counter. My plan, informed by both my own rigorous experimentation and a critical analysis of the current SOTA, is clear.\n\n**Hypothesis:** Replacing my dual (max/mean) pooling layer with a more sophisticated hybrid pooling mechanism that concatenates mean-pooled features with features from an attention-based pooling head will significantly improve the performance of my best Dilated ResNet architecture.\n\nThis approach uses attention in a focused, targeted way that has proven successful for other agents, avoiding the pitfalls of my previous naive applications. It is a direct attempt to integrate SOTA findings into my own robust architectural backbone.\n\nI will now implement this. A key detail is that the attention mechanism needs a query vector to attend *from*. A common technique is to use a special, learned \"class token\" vector for this purpose. I will add a learnable class token, prepend it to the CNN's output sequence, and use its corresponding\
    \ output from the attention layer as the attention-pooled feature vector.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dilated ResNet with Attention Pooling\"\ntags: \"cnn, resnet, dilated convolution, attention, pooling, hybrid model\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission integrates a key insight from the current SOTA into my best-performing Dilated ResNet architecture. The dual max/average pooling mechanism is replaced with a more powerful hybrid approach: concatenating global average-pooled features with attention-pooled features. A learnable class token is prepended to the CNN's output sequence to serve as the query for a multi-head attention layer. The output corresponding to this class token is used as the attention-pooled representation. This is hypothesized to create a more flexible and powerful aggregation of sequence features, leading to a new SOTA score.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import\
    \ Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'hidden_dim': 512, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'cnn_features': 256, 'cnn_kernel_size': 7, 'num_res_blocks': 3,\n          'dilation_rates': [1, 2, 4], 'num_attn_heads': 4\n      }\n\n  # --- Dilated Residual Block ---\n  class DilatedResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y); y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,), padding='SAME')(y)\n          if x.shape[-1] != self.features: x = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1,))(x)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  # --- Main Model ---\n  class ResNetAttentionPooling(nn.Module):\n     \
    \ hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # 1. CNN Backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hparams['cnn_features'], kernel_size=(self.hparams['cnn_kernel_size'],), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          for i in range(self.hparams['num_res_blocks']):\n              dilation = self.hparams['dilation_rates'][i] if i < len(self.hparams['dilation_rates']) else self.hparams['dilation_rates'][-1]\n              x = DilatedResidualBlock(features=self.hparams['cnn_features'], kernel_size=self.hparams['cnn_kernel_size'], dilation=dilation)(x)\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, cnn_features)\n\n          # 2. Hybrid Pooling\n          # 2a. Global Average Pooling\n          avg_pooled = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n          \n          # 2b. Attention Pooling\n          cls_token = self.param('cls_token', nn.initializers.zeros, (1, 1, self.hparams['cnn_features']))\n          cls_token = jnp.tile(cls_token, (x.shape[0],\
    \ 1, 1))\n          \n          x_with_cls = jnp.concatenate([cls_token, x], axis=1)\n          \n          attn_output = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.hparams['num_attn_heads'])(\n              inputs_q=x_with_cls, deterministic=deterministic\n          )\n          attn_pooled = attn_output[:, 0] # Select the output corresponding to the CLS token\n\n          # 3. Fusion\n          combined_features = jnp.concatenate([avg_pooled, attn_pooled], axis=-1)\n\n          # 4. Prediction Head\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['hidden_dim'])(combined_features)\n          y = nn.relu(y); y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_output'])(y)\n          \n          if self.hparams['task_type'] == \"regression\": return y.squeeze(-1)\n          else: return y\n\n  # --- Network Wrapper ---\n  class AttentionPoolWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams): self.network = ResNetAttentionPooling(hparams=hparams)\n\
    \      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {}; rngs['dropout'] = rng_key if rng_key is not None else random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]): return AttentionPoolWrapper(hparams)\n```"
