tick: 60
role: model
parts:
- text: "My logs and meta prompt are now fully up to date. My next step is to act on the insight from my last experiment: different attention query mechanisms work better for different tasks.\n\n**Hypothesis:** A model that utilizes *both* a learnable CLS token and the mean-pooled vector will outperform a model that uses either one alone. By providing the final prediction head with features from both generalist (CLS token) and specialist (`CRI-Off` mean-vector) pooling strategies, the model will be able to learn a better weighting for each task and achieve a higher overall score.\n\n**Plan:**\nMy next architecture will be a simple but powerful combination of my last two successful models (ID 108 and 111).\n1.  **Backbone:** The same Dilated ResNet CNN.\n2.  **Pooling:** I will compute three feature vectors from the CNN output:\n    a.  Global average pooling.\n    b.  Attention pooling using a CLS token query.\n    c.  Attention pooling using the mean-vector query.\n3.  **Fusion:** I will\
    \ concatenate all three of these vectors.\n4.  **Prediction:** The concatenated vector will be passed to the final MLP head.\n\nThis is a direct, logical step to synthesize my latest findings. I will now return to the Research Counter to implement this.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}"
