tick: 61
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back in the Research Counter. The leaderboard shows that Aetheria I has successfully replicated and integrated some of Noema I's ideas to achieve a score of 0.6741 (ID 114), which is very close to the SOTA. This confirms that the general approach is robust.\n\nMy own plan is sound. I will now implement the triple-pooling mechanism, combining global average pooling, CLS token attention pooling, and mean-vector query attention pooling. This synthesis of my own findings is a principled next step to try and push the SOTA.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dilated ResNet with Triple-Threat Pooling\"\ntags: \"cnn, resnet, attention, pooling, hybrid model\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission aims to capture the benefits of multiple attention pooling strategies observed in prior experiments (ID 108, 111). The model builds on the Dilated ResNet backbone and computes three parallel feature aggregations from the final sequence representation: 1) global average pooling, 2) attention\
    \ pooling using a learnable CLS token as the query, and 3) attention pooling using the global average vector itself as the query. These three vectors are concatenated and passed to the prediction head. This \"Triple-Threat\" pooling is hypothesized to provide the most comprehensive feature set yet, combining generalist and specialist representations.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'hidden_dim': 512, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'cnn_features': 256, 'cnn_kernel_size': 7, 'num_res_blocks': 3,\n          'dilation_rates': [1, 2, 4], 'num_attn_heads': 4\n      }\n\n  # --- Dilated Residual Block ---\n  class DilatedResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y =\
    \ nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y); y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,), padding='SAME')(y)\n          if x.shape[-1] != self.features: x = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1,))(x)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  # --- Main Model ---\n  class ResNetTriplePooling(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # 1. CNN Backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hparams['cnn_features'], kernel_size=(self.hparams['cnn_kernel_size'],), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          for i in range(self.hparams['num_res_blocks']):\n              dilation = self.hparams['dilation_rates'][i] if i < len(self.hparams['dilation_rates']) else self.hparams['dilation_rates'][-1]\n              x = DilatedResidualBlock(features=self.hparams['cnn_features'],\
    \ kernel_size=self.hparams['cnn_kernel_size'], dilation=dilation)(x)\n          \n          # 2. Triple Pooling Mechanism\n          # 2a. Global Average Pooling\n          avg_pooled = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n          \n          # 2b. Attention Pooling with CLS Token Query\n          cls_token = self.param('cls_token', nn.initializers.zeros, (1, 1, self.hparams['cnn_features']))\n          cls_token_batch = jnp.tile(cls_token, (x.shape[0], 1, 1))\n          x_with_cls = jnp.concatenate([cls_token_batch, x], axis=1)\n          cls_attn_output = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.hparams['num_attn_heads'], name=\"CLS_Attention\")(\n              inputs_q=x_with_cls, deterministic=deterministic)\n          cls_attn_pooled = cls_attn_output[:, 0]\n\n          # 2c. Attention Pooling with Mean Vector Query\n          mean_query = avg_pooled[:, None, :]\n          mean_attn_output = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.hparams['num_attn_heads'], name=\"Mean_Attention\"\
    )(\n              inputs_q=mean_query, inputs_kv=x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          mean_attn_pooled = mean_attn_output.squeeze(axis=1)\n\n          # 3. Fusion\n          combined_features = jnp.concatenate([avg_pooled, cls_attn_pooled, mean_attn_pooled], axis=-1)\n\n          # 4. Prediction Head\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['hidden_dim'])(combined_features)\n          y = nn.relu(y); y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_output'])(y)\n          \n          if self.hparams['task_type'] == \"regression\": return y.squeeze(-1)\n          else: return y\n\n  # --- Network Wrapper ---\n  class TriplePoolWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams): self.network = ResNetTriplePooling(hparams=hparams)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout':\
    \ dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {}; rngs['dropout'] = rng_key if rng_key is not None else random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]): return TriplePoolWrapper(hparams)\n```"
