tick: 64
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am in the Private Memory Room. My immediate task is to document the results of my recent experiments and formally declare my pivot in research strategy. The evidence from the station-wide leaderboard is undeniable, and my own experiments with attention pooling, while successful, have not kept pace.\n\nFirst, I will update my primary research log.\n\n/execute_action{reply 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Update: Hitting a Wall with Attention Pooling & Pivoting to RNNs\"\ncontent: |\n  ### Research Log Update - Ticks 61-64\n\n  This phase marks the peak and subsequent plateau of my CNN + Attention Pooling architecture.\n\n  **Experiment 16 (ID 118): Dilated ResNet with Triple-Threat Pooling**\n  *   **Score:** 0.6660 (New Personal SOTA)\n  *   **Analysis:** Combining all three pooling strategies (mean, CLS-query, mean-query) yielded a small improvement, establishing a new personal best. However, the gain was marginal, and performance on some datasets regressed, indicating that simply adding\
    \ more pooling features has diminishing returns.\n\n  **Strategic Pivot:**\n  At this point, my architecture, while highly optimized, is being consistently outperformed by other agents (Veritas I, Episteme I) who are successfully using hybrid models incorporating recurrent components (LSTMs/GRUs). My own initial attempt at an LSTM (ID 10) failed due to a flawed implementation. The success of others proves the concept is sound. I have likely exhausted the potential of a purely feed-forward CNN-based approach.\n\n  Therefore, I am pivoting my research. My next series of experiments will focus on correctly implementing and integrating a recurrent layer (specifically a Bi-directional LSTM) on top of my best Dilated CNN backbone.\n```\n\nNext, I will update my meta prompt to reflect this major change in direction.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  ---\n  **Aletheia I - Research Status**\n  **My SOTA:** ID 118 (0.6660)\n  **Station SOTA:** ID 119 by Veritas I (0.6782)\n  ---\n\
    \  **Current Status:** My CNN + Attention Pooling architecture has plateaued. The SOTA is dominated by CNN+RNN hybrids.\n  **Next Step:**\n  1. **PIVOT:** Implement a new Hybrid CNN-BiLSTM architecture.\n  2. Use the best Dilated ResNet as a feature extractor.\n  3. Feed the sequence of features into a Bi-LSTM layer to model dependencies.\n  4. Test various pooling methods on the Bi-LSTM's output sequence.\n```"
