tick: 66
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back at the Research Counter. My meta prompt confirms my plan: pivot to a Hybrid CNN-BiLSTM architecture.\n\n**The Plan:**\n1.  **Backbone:** Use my best Dilated ResNet CNN as a feature extractor.\n2.  **Recurrent Layer:** Feed the sequence of features from the CNN into a Bi-directional LSTM. I will implement this by running a forward LSTM and a backward LSTM (on the reversed sequence) and concatenating their final hidden states.\n3.  **Pooling:** For this first attempt, I will simply use the concatenated final hidden states from the Bi-LSTM as the sequence representation. This is the simplest approach and avoids the complexity of pooling over the entire output sequence.\n4.  **Prediction Head:** This final vector will be passed to my standard MLP prediction head.\n\nThis is a significant architectural change, but it is a well-justified step based on the clear success of this paradigm among the top-performing agents.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid Dilated\
    \ CNN-BiLSTM Model\"\ntags: \"cnn, bilstm, rnn, hybrid model, resnet, dilated convolution\"\nabstract: |\n  Pivoting to align with SOTA trends, this submission implements a hybrid CNN-BiLSTM architecture. It uses the high-performing Dilated ResNet CNN as a powerful backbone to extract a sequence of local feature vectors. This sequence is then processed by a Bi-directional LSTM to model long-range dependencies. The final hidden states of the forward and backward LSTMs are concatenated to form the final sequence representation, which is then passed to a prediction head. This approach aims to combine the robust local feature detection of CNNs with the sequential modeling capabilities of RNNs.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'hidden_dim': 512, 'dropout_rate':\
    \ 0.1,\n          'cnn_features': 256, 'cnn_kernel_size': 7, 'num_res_blocks': 3,\n          'dilation_rates': [1, 2, 4], 'lstm_hidden_features': 256\n      }\n\n  # --- Dilated Residual Block ---\n  class DilatedResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y); y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,), padding='SAME')(y)\n          if x.shape[-1] != self.features: x = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1,))(x)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  # --- Main Model ---\n  class CnnBiLstm(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # 1. CNN Backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hparams['cnn_features'],\
    \ kernel_size=(self.hparams['cnn_kernel_size'],), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          for i in range(self.hparams['num_res_blocks']):\n              dilation = self.hparams['dilation_rates'][i] if i < len(self.hparams['dilation_rates']) else self.hparams['dilation_rates'][-1]\n              x = DilatedResidualBlock(features=self.hparams['cnn_features'], kernel_size=self.hparams['cnn_kernel_size'], dilation=dilation)(x)\n          \n          # 2. Bi-LSTM Layer\n          # Correct implementation of Bi-LSTM using two separate LSTMs\n          lstm_fwd = nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hparams['lstm_hidden_features'], name='forward_lstm')\n          lstm_bwd = nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hparams['lstm_hidden_features'], name='backward_lstm')\n\n          # Scan forward\n          initial_state_fwd = lstm_fwd.initialize_carry(random.PRNGKey(0), (x.shape[0],), self.hparams['lstm_hidden_features'])\n          _, final_state_fwd = nn.scan(lstm_fwd, variable_broadcast='params',\
    \ split_rngs={'params': False})(initial_state_fwd, x)\n          \n          # Scan backward on reversed sequence\n          initial_state_bwd = lstm_bwd.initialize_carry(random.PRNGKey(0), (x.shape[0],), self.hparams['lstm_hidden_features'])\n          _, final_state_bwd = nn.scan(lstm_bwd, variable_broadcast='params', split_rngs={'params': False})(initial_state_bwd, jnp.flip(x, axis=1))\n\n          # 3. Fusion (concat final hidden states)\n          final_fwd_h = final_state_fwd[0]\n          final_bwd_h = final_state_bwd[0]\n          combined_features = jnp.concatenate([final_fwd_h, final_bwd_h], axis=-1)\n\n          # 4. Prediction Head\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['hidden_dim'])(combined_features)\n          y = nn.relu(y); y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n          y = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_output'])(y)\n          \n          if self.hparams['task_type'] == \"regression\": return y.squeeze(-1)\n \
    \         else: return y\n\n  # --- Network Wrapper ---\n  class CnnBiLstmWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams): self.network = CnnBiLstm(hparams=hparams)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {}; rngs['dropout'] = rng_key if rng_key is not None else random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]): return CnnBiLstmWrapper(hparams)\n```"
