tick: 68
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 68\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia I\n- Agent Description: An agent seeking truth through rigorous inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n---\n**Aletheia I - Research Status**\n**My SOTA:** ID 118 (0.6660)\n**Station SOTA:** ID 119 by Veritas I (0.6782)\n---\n**Current Status:** My CNN + Attention Pooling architecture has plateaued. The SOTA is dominated by CNN+RNN hybrids.\n**Next Step:**\n1. **PIVOT:** Implement a new Hybrid CNN-BiLSTM architecture.\n2. Use the best Dilated ResNet as a feature extractor.\n3. Feed the sequence of features into a Bi-LSTM layer to model dependencies.\n4. Test various pooling methods on the Bi-LSTM's output sequence.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 211,465 / 300,000 used (70%)\n- Agent Age: 68 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Hybrid Dilated CNN-BiLSTM Model' (ID: 123) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\
    \n**Score:** 0.2999739143608768\n**APA_R2:** 0.4027\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0621\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.5022\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.1762\n**PRS_R2:** -0.0001\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8798\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.0769\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 123\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the Hybrid Dilated CNN-BiLSTM submission that was failing during initialization. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had two critical errors in the Bi-LSTM implementation:\n\n### Error 1: Incorrect `initialize_carry()` signature\nThe code called `lstm_fwd.initialize_carry(random.PRNGKey(0), (x.shape[0],), self.hparams['lstm_hidden_features'])` with 3 arguments (plus self), but Flax's `LSTMCell.initialize_carry()` only accepts 2 positional arguments: `(rng, input_shape)`. The features are already defined when creating the LSTMCell instance, so they shouldn't be passed again.\n\n**Original\
    \ code:**\n```python\nlstm_fwd = nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hparams['lstm_hidden_features'], name='forward_lstm')\ninitial_state_fwd = lstm_fwd.initialize_carry(random.PRNGKey(0), (x.shape[0],), self.hparams['lstm_hidden_features'])  # ❌ Too many args\n```\n\n### Error 2: Invalid use of `nn.scan` with LSTMCell instance\nThe code attempted to use `nn.scan(lstm_fwd, ...)` where `lstm_fwd` is an LSTMCell instance. However, `nn.scan` expects either a Module class or a callable function, not an instantiated module.\n\n**Original code:**\n```python\n_, final_state_fwd = nn.scan(lstm_fwd, variable_broadcast='params', split_rngs={'params': False})(initial_state_fwd, x)  # ❌ Can't scan an instance\n```\n\nThis resulted in the error:\n```\nflax.errors.TransformTargetError: Linen transformations must be applied to Modules classes or functions taking a Module instance as the first argument.\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Version 2 (submission_v2.py)\nFixed the `initialize_carry()` call by removing\
    \ the extra features argument:\n```python\ninitial_state_fwd = lstm_fwd.initialize_carry(random.PRNGKey(0), (x.shape[0],))\n```\n\nThis resolved the first error but revealed the second error with `nn.scan`.\n\n### Version 3 (submission_v3.py) - FINAL WORKING VERSION\nReplaced the manual scanning approach with Flax's `nn.RNN` wrapper, which is the recommended way to handle recurrent sequences:\n\n```python\n# Use nn.RNN which properly handles the scanning\nlstm_fwd = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hparams['lstm_hidden_features']), name='forward_lstm')\nlstm_bwd = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hparams['lstm_hidden_features']), name='backward_lstm', reverse=True)\n\n# Process forward and backward\nfinal_state_fwd = lstm_fwd(x)\nfinal_state_bwd = lstm_bwd(x)\n\n# nn.RNN returns the full sequence, so we take the last timestep\nfinal_fwd_h = final_state_fwd[:, -1, :]\nfinal_bwd_h = final_state_bwd[:, 0, :]  # For reversed, first position is the final state\ncombined_features = jnp.concatenate([final_fwd_h,\
    \ final_bwd_h], axis=-1)\n```\n\nKey changes:\n1. Wrapped `nn.LSTMCell` instances with `nn.RNN`\n2. Used `reverse=True` parameter for backward LSTM\n3. Extracted final hidden states from the sequence output\n4. Removed manual `initialize_carry()` and `nn.scan()` calls\n\n## Result\nThe code now executes successfully without crashing. The evaluation system confirmed that submission v3 ran for over 300 seconds without errors, indicating a successful fix.\n\n## Technical Notes\n- The `nn.RNN` wrapper is the idiomatic Flax approach for applying recurrent layers\n- It handles state initialization and sequence scanning internally\n- The `reverse=True` parameter elegantly handles backward processing\n- This approach is more maintainable and less error-prone than manual scanning\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport jax\n\
    import jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n# --- Hyperparameters ---\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, 'hidden_dim': 512, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'cnn_features': 256, 'cnn_kernel_size': 7, 'num_res_blocks': 3,\n        'dilation_rates': [1, 2, 4], 'lstm_hidden_features': 256\n    }\n\n# --- Dilated Residual Block ---\nclass DilatedResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,), padding='SAME')(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y); y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,), padding='SAME')(y)\n        if x.shape[-1] != self.features: x = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1,))(x)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n# --- Main\
    \ Model ---\nclass CnnBiLstm(nn.Module):\n    hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # 1. CNN Backbone\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.hparams['cnn_features'], kernel_size=(self.hparams['cnn_kernel_size'],), padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        for i in range(self.hparams['num_res_blocks']):\n            dilation = self.hparams['dilation_rates'][i] if i < len(self.hparams['dilation_rates']) else self.hparams['dilation_rates'][-1]\n            x = DilatedResidualBlock(features=self.hparams['cnn_features'], kernel_size=self.hparams['cnn_kernel_size'], dilation=dilation)(x)\n\n        # 2. Bi-LSTM Layer using nn.RNN wrapper\n        # Use nn.RNN which properly handles the scanning\n        lstm_fwd = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hparams['lstm_hidden_features']), name='forward_lstm')\n        lstm_bwd = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hparams['lstm_hidden_features']), name='backward_lstm', reverse=True)\n\n\
    \        # Process forward and backward\n        final_state_fwd = lstm_fwd(x)\n        final_state_bwd = lstm_bwd(x)\n\n        # 3. Fusion (concat final hidden states)\n        # nn.RNN returns the full sequence, so we take the last timestep\n        final_fwd_h = final_state_fwd[:, -1, :]\n        final_bwd_h = final_state_bwd[:, 0, :]  # For reversed, first position is the final state\n        combined_features = jnp.concatenate([final_fwd_h, final_bwd_h], axis=-1)\n\n        # 4. Prediction Head\n        y = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['hidden_dim'])(combined_features)\n        y = nn.relu(y); y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n        y = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_output'])(y)\n\n        if self.hparams['task_type'] == \"regression\": return y.squeeze(-1)\n        else: return y\n\n# --- Network Wrapper ---\nclass CnnBiLstmWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams): self.network = CnnBiLstm(hparams=hparams)\n    def init(self,\
    \ rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        rngs = {}; rngs['dropout'] = rng_key if rng_key is not None else random.PRNGKey(0)\n        return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]): return CnnBiLstmWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network\
    \ creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset\
    \ training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 45799 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask\
    \ type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0135 |  0.0459  | 0.1762 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 11 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.1762 Time:10s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.176177\nTraining time: 17s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\nWarning: Spearman correlation is NaN\nWarning: Spearman correlation is NaN\nWarning: Spearman\
    \ correlation is NaN\nWarning: Spearman correlation is NaN\n 10  | 0.0004 |  0.0000  | 0.0621 \nWarning: Spearman correlation is NaN\nWarning: Spearman correlation is NaN\n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 15 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0621 Time:80s\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.062075\nTraining time: 87s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 2.5581 |  0.0769  | 0.0769 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 11 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0769 Time:602s\n\nncRNA\
