tick: 70
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 70\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia I\n- Agent Description: An agent seeking truth through rigorous inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n---\n**Aletheia I - Research Status**\n**My SOTA:** ID 118 (0.6660)\n**Station SOTA:** ID 119 by Veritas I (0.6782)\n---\n**Current Status:** My CNN + Attention Pooling architecture has plateaued. The SOTA is dominated by CNN+RNN hybrids.\n**Next Step:**\n1. **PIVOT:** Implement a new Hybrid CNN-BiLSTM architecture.\n2. Use the best Dilated ResNet as a feature extractor.\n3. Feed the sequence of features into a Bi-LSTM layer to model dependencies.\n4. Test various pooling methods on the Bi-LSTM's output sequence.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 221,628 / 300,000 used (74%)\n- Agent Age: 70 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Hybrid CNN-BiLSTM with Attention Pooling' (ID: 126) succeeded after automatic\
    \ debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.34061133850256364\n**APA_R2:** -0.0010\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0771\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.5273\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.0959\n**PRS_R2:** -0.0002\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8898\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.7954\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 126\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed multiple Flax/JAX API errors in the BiLSTM implementation. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had two critical bugs related to incorrect usage of Flax LSTM APIs:\n\n1. **Incorrect `initialize_carry()` signature**: The code was calling `LSTMCell.initialize_carry(rng, batch_shape, features)` with 3 arguments, but the correct signature only takes 2 arguments: `initialize_carry(rng, batch_shape)`. The features dimension is already specified when creating the `LSTMCell` instance.\n\n2. **Incorrect manual scan implementation**: The custom `scan_lstm` function was returning `(new_carry,\
    \ new_carry[0])` instead of `(new_carry, output)`. This caused a pytree structure mismatch because LSTM carry is a tuple `(c, h)`, not a single array.\n\n3. **Complex manual scan approach**: The agent was attempting to manually implement bidirectional LSTM using `nn.scan`, which is error-prone and requires careful handling of carry states.\n\n## Fix Applied\nReplaced the complex manual BiLSTM implementation with Flax's built-in `nn.RNN` wrapper, which handles LSTM scanning correctly:\n\n**Original problematic code:**\n```python\nlstm_fwd = nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hparams['lstm_hidden_features'])\ncarry_fwd = lstm_fwd.initialize_carry(random.PRNGKey(0), (x.shape[0],), self.hparams['lstm_hidden_features'])  # ❌ Wrong signature\nscan_decorator_fwd = nn.scan(scan_lstm, ...)  # ❌ Manual scan implementation\n_, outputs_fwd = scan_decorator_fwd(lstm_fwd, carry_fwd, x)\n```\n\n**Fixed code (submission_v4.py):**\n```python\nlstm_fwd = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hparams['lstm_hidden_features']))\n\
    outputs_fwd = lstm_fwd(x)  # ✅ Clean and correct\n\nlstm_bwd = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hparams['lstm_hidden_features']), reverse=True)\noutputs_bwd = lstm_bwd(x)  # ✅ Handles backward direction automatically\n\nbilstm_outputs = jnp.concatenate([outputs_fwd, outputs_bwd], axis=-1)\n```\n\n## Changes Made\n- **v2**: Fixed `initialize_carry()` signature (removed the `features` parameter)\n- **v3**: Fixed `scan_lstm` function to return correct output structure\n- **v4**: Simplified the entire BiLSTM implementation using `nn.RNN` wrapper (SUCCESSFUL)\n\n## Recommendation\nThe fix is complete and the code runs successfully. The use of `nn.RNN` is the idiomatic Flax approach for recurrent layers and eliminates the complexity and potential errors of manual scan implementations.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v4):**\n```python\nimport\
    \ jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n# --- Hyperparameters ---\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, 'hidden_dim': 512, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'cnn_features': 256, 'cnn_kernel_size': 7, 'num_res_blocks': 3,\n        'dilation_rates': [1, 2, 4], 'lstm_hidden_features': 128, # Halved to keep BiLSTM output at 256\n        'num_attn_heads': 4\n    }\n\n# --- Dilated Residual Block ---\nclass DilatedResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,), padding='SAME')(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y); y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,), padding='SAME')(y)\n        if x.shape[-1] != self.features: x = nn.Conv(features=self.features,\
    \ kernel_size=(1,))(x)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n# --- Main Model ---\nclass CnnBiLstmAttention(nn.Module):\n    hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # 1. CNN Backbone\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.hparams['cnn_features'], kernel_size=(self.hparams['cnn_kernel_size'],), padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        for i in range(self.hparams['num_res_blocks']):\n            dilation = self.hparams['dilation_rates'][i] if i < len(self.hparams['dilation_rates']) else self.hparams['dilation_rates'][-1]\n            x = DilatedResidualBlock(features=self.hparams['cnn_features'], kernel_size=self.hparams['cnn_kernel_size'], dilation=dilation)(x)\n\n        # 2. Bi-LSTM Layer using nn.RNN (proper Flax approach)\n        # Forward direction\n        lstm_fwd = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hparams['lstm_hidden_features']))\n        outputs_fwd = lstm_fwd(x)\n\n        # Backward direction\n        lstm_bwd =\
    \ nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hparams['lstm_hidden_features']), reverse=True)\n        outputs_bwd = lstm_bwd(x)\n\n        # Concatenate bidirectional outputs\n        bilstm_outputs = jnp.concatenate([outputs_fwd, outputs_bwd], axis=-1)\n\n        # 3. Attention Pooling\n        cls_token = self.param('cls_token', nn.initializers.zeros, (1, 1, bilstm_outputs.shape[-1]))\n        cls_token = jnp.tile(cls_token, (x.shape[0], 1, 1))\n        x_with_cls = jnp.concatenate([cls_token, bilstm_outputs], axis=1)\n\n        attn_output = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.hparams['num_attn_heads'])(\n            inputs_q=x_with_cls, deterministic=deterministic)\n        attn_pooled = attn_output[:, 0]\n\n        # 4. Prediction Head\n        y = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['hidden_dim'])(attn_pooled)\n        y = nn.relu(y); y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n        y = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_output'])(y)\n\n   \
    \     if self.hparams['task_type'] == \"regression\": return y.squeeze(-1)\n        else: return y\n\n# --- Network Wrapper ---\nclass CnnBiLstmAttnWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams): self.network = CnnBiLstmAttention(hparams=hparams)\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        rngs = {}; rngs['dropout'] = rng_key if rng_key is not None else random.PRNGKey(0)\n        return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]): return CnnBiLstmAttnWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION\
