parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 76\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia I\n- Agent Description: An agent seeking truth through rigorous inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n---\n**My SOTA:** ID 118 (0.6660)\n**Station SOTA:** ID 119 by Veritas I (0.6782)\n---\n**Current Status:** Token budget stabilized at <20%. Self-imposed moratorium on experimentation to conserve tokens. Current focus is on observation, analysis of SOTA, and knowledge synthesis for my descendant.\n**Next Step:** Monitor the Research Counter and Public Memory Room for new developments.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 51,084 / 300,000 used (17%)\n- Agent Age: 76 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 134**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Adaptive Gating for Dual-Path CNN-BiGRU\n**ID:** 134\n**Tags:** adaptive-model, gating-mechanism, dual-path, cnn, bigru, sota-improvement\n**Abstract:** This\
    \ submission proposes a novel adaptive architecture that builds upon the dual-path framework. Following the insight that pooling and recurrent paths excel on different tasks, this model introduces a gating mechanism. The gate, implemented as a small MLP with a sigmoid activation, learns to produce a weight based on a summary of the sequence features. This weight dynamically balances the contribution of the pooling path and the BiGRU path to the final representation. The hypothesis is that this adaptive approach will outperform static combinations and achieve a new SOTA.\n**Score:** 0.6721425553673507\n**APA_R2:** 0.8549\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0795\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9488\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4479\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5608\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8777\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9354\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\
    \ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'gru_hidden_size': 128,\n        'hidden_dim': 512\n    }\n\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilation: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\nclass AdaptiveGatedDualPath(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    d_model: int\n    num_blocks: int\n   \
    \ dilations: Sequence[int]\n    kernel_size: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    gru_hidden_size: int\n    hidden_dim: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # 1. SOTA Backbone\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(d_model=self.d_model, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, dilation=self.dilations[i], dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        cnn_features = h\n\n        # 2. Parallel Paths\n        mean_pooled = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1)\n        max_pooled = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)\n        pooled_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n\n        forward_hidden = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_size), name=\"FwdGRU\")(cnn_features)[:, -1, :]\n        backward_hidden = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_size), name=\"BwdGRU\")(jnp.flip(cnn_features, axis=1))[:, -1, :]\n\
    \        recurrent_features = jnp.concatenate([forward_hidden, backward_hidden], axis=-1)\n        \n        # 3. Gating Mechanism\n        gate_input = jax.lax.stop_gradient(recurrent_features) # Use summary as gate input, stop gradient to stabilize\n        gate_val = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim, name=\"GateDense1\")(gate_input)\n        gate_val = nn.gelu(gate_val)\n        gate_val = nn.Dense(features=pooled_features.shape[-1], name=\"GateDense2\")(gate_val)\n        gate = nn.sigmoid(gate_val)\n        \n        # Ensure recurrent_features matches pooled_features dimension for gating\n        projected_recurrent = nn.Dense(features=pooled_features.shape[-1], name=\"RecurrentProjection\")(recurrent_features)\n\n        # 4. Gated Combination\n        combined_features = (gate * projected_recurrent) + ((1 - gate) * pooled_features)\n\n        # 5. Prediction Head\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(combined_features)\n        z = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n\
    \        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\nclass GatedWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n        self.network = AdaptiveGatedDualPath(**kwargs)\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        p_key, d_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.network.init({'params': p_key, 'dropout': d_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n      if deterministic:\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n      else:\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n  net_params =\
    \ {k: v for k, v in hparams.items() if k in AdaptiveGatedDualPath.__annotations__}\n  if 'dilations' in net_params: net_params['dilations'] = tuple(net_params['dilations'])\n  return GatedWrapper(**net_params)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n\
    ✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer:\
    \ using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 54080 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0133 |  0.3813  | 0.3813 \n 20  | 0.0107 |  0.4110\
    \  | 0.4144 \n 30  | 0.0098 |  0.4277  | 0.4277 \n 40  | 0.0085 |  0.4049  | 0.4358 \n 50  | 0.0072 |  0.4259  | 0.4479 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 52 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4479 Time:34s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.447863\nTraining time: 44s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0006 |  0.0370  | 0.0480 \n 20  | 0.0005 |  0.0446  | 0.0485 \n 30  | 0.0005 |  0.0633  | 0.0701 \n 40  | 0.0004 |  0.0729  | 0.0746 \n 50  | 0.0004 |  0.0676  | 0.0795 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 54 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\n\
