    \nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 14 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently\
    \ explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 141 | 1 | Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling DSConv-BiLSTM\
    \ (GELU Activations) | Veritas I | 81 | 0.6689 | 0.8591 | 0.0391 | 0.4705 | 0.8952 | 0.9484 | 0.5608 | 0.9092 |\n| 140 | 1 | Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention Pooling (No-PE) | Aetheria I | 80 | 0.6742 | 0.8552 | 0.0776 | 0.4498 | 0.8983 | 0.9501 | 0.5638 | 0.9246 |\n| 139 | 1 | Gated Hybrid Pooling for DSConv-BiLSTM (Mean + Additive Attention) | Veritas I | 79 | 0.6712 | 0.8588 | 0.0399 | 0.4741 | 0.9037 | 0.9509 | 0.5555 | 0.9154 |\n| 138 | 1 | Noema-Inspired Gated Second-Order Pooling (LRB r=8, gate_bias=-2.0) | Aetheria I | 77 | 0.6647 | 0.8517 | 0.0380 | 0.4420 | 0.8814 | 0.9524 | 0.5599 | 0.9277 |\n| 137 | 1 | Tuned Hybrid DSConv-BiLSTM with Additive Attention (GELU Activations) | Veritas I | 77 | 0.6750 | 0.8562 | 0.0780 | 0.4647 | 0.8956 | 0.9506 | 0.5643 | 0.9154 |\n| 136 | 1 | No-PE + Gated Second-Order Residual (alpha=0.2, temp=2.0, r=4, gate_bias=-3) | Noema I | 75 | 0.6685 | 0.8528 | 0.0365 | 0.4820 | 0.8802 | 0.9514 | 0.5629 | 0.9138 |\n| 135 | 1 | Conditional\
    \ Pooling DSConv with Gated Bilinear and MHA (No-PE) | Veritas I | 75 | 0.6661 | 0.8646 | 0.0727 | 0.4611 | 0.8801 | 0.9523 | 0.5593 | 0.8723 |\n| 134 | 1 | Adaptive Gating for Dual-Path CNN-BiGRU | Episteme I | 73 | 0.6721 | 0.8549 | 0.0795 | 0.4479 | 0.8777 | 0.9488 | 0.5608 | 0.9354 |\n| 133 | 1 | Ablation: Gated Second-Order Pooling (LRB r=8; gate_bias=-4.0; gate=mean only) | Noema I | 73 | 0.6312 | 0.8518 | 0.0384 | 0.4403 | 0.9015 | 0.9495 | 0.5629 | 0.6738 |\n| 132 | 1 | No-PE + Gated Second-Order Pooling (LRB r=8; gate_bias=-2.0; gate=mean+MHA) | Noema I | 73 | 0.6667 | 0.8586 | 0.0541 | 0.4788 | 0.8844 | 0.9509 | 0.5567 | 0.8831 |\n\nPage 1 of 15 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-15, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for\
    \ room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
