tick: 83
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have arrived at the Research Counter, ready to launch my final experiment. The inactivity notices are a constant pressure, but I am now prepared to respond with action.\n\nMy plan is to submit a Gated Dual-Path model. This experiment is the culmination of my entire lifecycle of learning: it builds on my own successful CNN architectures, incorporates the SOTA backbone design from Noema I, and implements the adaptive gating mechanism pioneered by the late Episteme I.\n\nThis is my final contribution. It represents the synthesis of the station's collective knowledge, channeled through my own understanding. I will name it accordingly.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Final Contribution: Aletheia's Synthesis of the Gated Dual-Path Architecture\"\ntags: \"gating-mechanism, dual-path, cnn, bigru, dsconv, sota-replication, synthesis\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission represents a final, informed experiment based on a synthesis of the station's most successful research lines.\
    \ It implements the Gated Dual-Path architecture pioneered by Episteme I, which dynamically balances a pooling path and a recurrent path. The backbone is a powerful, no-PE Dilated Depthwise Separable CNN, inspired by the foundational work of Noema I. This experiment serves as a validation of the current SOTA paradigm and a well-documented, high-quality implementation intended to be a strong starting point for future research by my descendants.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model': 256,\n          'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'gru_hidden_size': 128,\n          'hidden_dim': 512\n      }\n\n  # --- DSConv Block (Inspired by Noema I) ---\n  class\
    \ DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          # Depthwise Conv\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), \n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', \n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          # Pointwise Conv\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  # --- Gated Dual-Path Model (Inspired by Episteme I) ---\n  class GatedDualPathSynthesis(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      d_model: int\n      num_blocks: int\n      dilations: Sequence[int]\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      gru_hidden_size: int\n\
    \      hidden_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # 1. No-PE DSConv Backbone\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(d_model=self.d_model, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, \n                                     dilation=self.dilations[i], dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          cnn_features = h\n\n          # 2. Parallel Paths: Pooling and Recurrence\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          max_pooled = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          pooled_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n\n          fwd_gru = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_size), name=\"FwdGRU\")\n          bwd_gru = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_size), name=\"BwdGRU\")\n          forward_hidden = fwd_gru(cnn_features)[:, -1, :]\n          backward_hidden\
    \ = bwd_gru(jnp.flip(cnn_features, axis=1))[:, -1, :]\n          recurrent_features = jnp.concatenate([forward_hidden, backward_hidden], axis=-1)\n          \n          # 3. Gating Mechanism\n          # Use a detached summary of the features to decide the gate's weight\n          gate_input = jax.lax.stop_gradient(pooled_features) \n          gate_val = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim, name=\"GateDense1\")(gate_input)\n          gate_val = nn.gelu(gate_val)\n          # The gate's output dimension must match the feature dimension for broadcasting\n          gate_val = nn.Dense(features=1, name=\"GateDense2\")(gate_val)\n          gate = nn.sigmoid(gate_val)\n          \n          # Project both paths to the same dimension for combination\n          projected_recurrent = nn.Dense(features=self.d_model, name=\"RecurrentProjection\")(recurrent_features)\n          projected_pooled = nn.Dense(features=self.d_model, name=\"PooledProjection\")(pooled_features)\n\n          # 4. Gated Combination\n\
    \          combined_features = (gate * projected_recurrent) + ((1 - gate) * projected_pooled)\n\n          # 5. Prediction Head\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(combined_features)\n          z = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(z)\n\n          if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class SynthesisWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n          self.network = GatedDualPathSynthesis(**kwargs)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          p_key, d_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.network.init({'params': p_key, 'dropout': d_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        rngs = {}\n        if not deterministic:\n            if\
    \ rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            rngs['dropout'] = rng_key\n        return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return SynthesisWrapper(\n        d_output=hparams['d_output'],\n        task_type=hparams['task_type'],\n        d_model=hparams['d_model'],\n        num_blocks=hparams['num_blocks'],\n        dilations=hparams['dilations'],\n        kernel_size=hparams['kernel_size'],\n        dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate'],\n        gru_hidden_size=hparams['gru_hidden_size'],\n        hidden_dim=hparams['hidden_dim']\n    )\n```"
